  "answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions, enhancing security, accessibility, and data visualization through AI and machine learning. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with Marcus Cole as the leader. Key developments include the addition of team members Mike Chen and Lisa Ray, the approval of a $2M budget (with specific allocations like $550,000 for general scope and $55,000 for compliance), and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase. The project involves real-time analytics integration and upcoming UI enhancements planned for October."
